/-!
# Simple spheres

A map `u` out of the Riemann sphere `OnePoint ℂ` is **multiply covered** when it factors as
`u = v ∘ φ` through a holomorphic map `φ` of the sphere to itself of degree greater than one, and
a nonconstant map which is not multiply covered is **simple** (`TauCeti.IsSimpleSphere`). The
moduli spaces of pseudoholomorphic spheres are built from simple spheres, and the dimension count
and the transversality theory apply to them; a multiply covered sphere is handled through the
simple sphere it covers.

The holomorphic maps of the sphere to itself are the finite holomorphic maps
`TauCeti.RiemannSurface.FiniteHolomorphicMap (OnePoint ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ)`, with their degree
`TauCeti.RiemannSurface.degree`. No regularity is imposed on the factor `v`: the map `u` factors
through `φ` exactly when it is constant on the fibres of `φ`, so simplicity is a condition on the
fibres of `u` alone and makes sense for every map. For a pseudoholomorphic `u`, a factor `v` is
pseudoholomorphic away from the finitely many branch values of `φ`, where `φ` has local
holomorphic inverses.

The results are the following.

* **Injective points.** If `u` is injective on a neighbourhood of a point `z` and no other point
  has the image `u z`, then `u` is simple (`TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_of_injOn`): through such a point
  any factor `φ` is a finite holomorphic map with an injective point, hence of degree one
  (`TauCeti.RiemannSurface.degree_eq_one_of_injOn`). For a pseudoholomorphic sphere, local
  injectivity holds at every point where its derivative does not vanish
  (`ContMDiffAt.exists_mem_nhds_injOn`), so a sphere with an injective regular point is simple.
* **Möbius invariance.** Precomposing with a Möbius transformation preserves simplicity
  (`TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_comp_smul_iff`), since a Möbius transformation is a finite holomorphic
  map of degree one (`TauCeti.RiemannSurface.FiniteHolomorphicMap.ofPSL`). So simplicity is a
  property of the unparametrized sphere.
* **Holomorphic self-maps.** A finite holomorphic map of the sphere to itself is simple exactly
  when it has degree one (`TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_iff_degree_eq_one`); for instance the power map
  `z ↦ z ^ n`, `n ≥ 2`, is not simple (`TauCeti.not_isSimpleSphere_onePointMap_pow`).
* **Trivial stabilizers.** A Möbius transformation `g` with `u ∘ (g • ·) = u`, for a continuous
  simple sphere `u` with values in a Hausdorff space, is the identity
  (`TauCeti.IsSimpleSphere.eq_one_of_forall_apply_smul_eq`), so the reparametrization action of
  `PSL(2, ℂ)` is free on continuous simple spheres
  (`TauCeti.IsSimpleSphere.eq_of_forall_apply_smul_eq_apply_smul`). After conjugating a fixed point
  of `g` to `∞`, the transformation `g` is affine. A continuous map invariant under a nonzero
  translation, or under a dilation `z ↦ a z` with `|a| ≠ 1`, is constant, as the iterates of
  every point converge to a single point. A map invariant under a rotation `z ↦ a z` with
  `|a| = 1` and `a ≠ 1` is invariant under all the `n`-th roots of unity for some `n ≥ 2`: those
  generated by `a` when `a` has finite order, and `±1` otherwise, since the powers of `a` are then
  dense in the circle. Such a map factors through `z ↦ z ^ n`
  (`TauCeti.exists_eq_comp_onePointMap_pow`) and is not simple.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.IsSimpleSphere`: simple maps of the Riemann sphere.
* `TauCeti.not_isSimpleSphere_comp`: a map factoring through a self-map of the sphere of degree
  greater than one is not simple.
* `TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_of_injOn`: a map with an injective point is simple.
* `TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_comp_smul_iff`: simplicity is invariant under reparametrization.
* `TauCeti.isSimpleSphere_iff_degree_eq_one`: the simple holomorphic self-maps of the sphere are
  the maps of degree one.
* `TauCeti.IsSimpleSphere.eq_one_of_forall_apply_smul_eq`: continuous simple spheres have trivial
  stabilizers in `PSL(2, ℂ)`.

## References

* D. McDuff and D. Salamon, *J-holomorphic Curves and Symplectic Topology*, 2nd ed., American
  Mathematical Society Colloquium Publications 52, 2012, §2.5 (simple curves and multiple covers).
* C. Wendl, *Lectures on holomorphic curves in symplectic and contact geometry*,
  arXiv:1011.1690, Definitions 4.4 and 4.5 (simple and multiply covered curves).
-/

public section

open Filter Function OnePoint Set Topology
open scoped ContDiff Manifold MatrixGroups

namespace TauCeti

open RiemannSurface Matrix.ProjectiveSpecialLinearGroup

variable {X : Type*} {u : OnePoint ℂ → X}

/-- A map `u` from the Riemann sphere is a **simple sphere** when it takes two distinct values and
does not factor through a holomorphic map of the sphere to itself of degree greater than one:
whenever `u = v ∘ φ` for a finite holomorphic map `φ` of the sphere, `φ` has degree one. No
regularity is asked of `v`, so `u` factors through `φ` exactly when it is constant on the fibres of
`φ`. -/
structure IsSimpleSphere (u : OnePoint ℂ → X) : Prop where
  /-- A simple sphere takes two distinct values. -/
  nonconstant : ∃ z w, u z ≠ u w
  /-- A simple sphere factors only through finite holomorphic maps of degree one. -/
  degree_eq_one (φ : FiniteHolomorphicMap (OnePoint ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ)) (v : OnePoint ℂ → X) :
    u = v ∘ φ → degree φ = 1

/-- A map factoring through a holomorphic map of the sphere to itself of degree greater than one is
not simple. -/
theorem not_isSimpleSphere_comp {φ : FiniteHolomorphicMap (OnePoint ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ)}
    (hφ : 1 < degree φ) (v : OnePoint ℂ → X) : ¬IsSimpleSphere (v ∘ φ) :=
  fun h ↦ hφ.ne' (h.degree_eq_one φ v rfl)

/-- **A map with an injective point is simple.** If `u` is injective on a neighbourhood `t` of `z`
and no other point has the image `u z`, then `u` is a simple sphere. -/
theorem isSimpleSphere_of_injOn {z : OnePoint ℂ} {t : Set (OnePoint ℂ)} (ht : t ∈ 𝓝 z)
    (hinj : InjOn u t) (hfib : ∀ w, u w = u z → w = z) : IsSimpleSphere u where
  nonconstant := by
    obtain ⟨w, -, hwz⟩ := ((infinite_of_mem_nhds z ht).sdiff (finite_singleton z)).nonempty
    exact ⟨w, z, fun h ↦ hwz (hfib w h)⟩
  degree_eq_one φ v huv := by
    subst huv
    exact degree_eq_one_of_injOn φ ht hinj.of_comp fun w h ↦ hfib w (congrArg v h)

/-- Precomposing a simple sphere with a Möbius transformation gives a simple sphere. -/
theorem IsSimpleSphere.comp_smul (hu : IsSimpleSphere u) (g : PSL(2, ℂ)) :
    IsSimpleSphere fun z ↦ u (g • z) where
  nonconstant := by
    obtain ⟨z, w, h⟩ := hu.nonconstant
    exact ⟨g⁻¹ • z, g⁻¹ • w, by simpa using h⟩
  degree_eq_one φ v huv := by
    have h := hu.degree_eq_one (φ.comp (FiniteHolomorphicMap.ofPSL g⁻¹)) v (funext fun z ↦ by
      simpa using congrFun huv (g⁻¹ • z))
    rwa [degree_comp, FiniteHolomorphicMap.coe_ofPSL, degree_psl_smul, mul_one] at h

/-- **Simplicity is invariant under reparametrization** by Möbius transformations. -/
@[simp]
theorem isSimpleSphere_comp_smul_iff (g : PSL(2, ℂ)) :
    (IsSimpleSphere fun z ↦ u (g • z)) ↔ IsSimpleSphere u :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ by simpa using h.comp_smul g⁻¹, fun h ↦ h.comp_smul g⟩

/-- **A holomorphic map of the sphere to itself is simple exactly when it has degree one.** A map
of degree one is injective, so each of its points is injective; a map of degree greater than one
factors through itself. -/
theorem isSimpleSphere_iff_degree_eq_one (φ : FiniteHolomorphicMap (OnePoint ℂ) (OnePoint ℂ)) :
    IsSimpleSphere ⇑φ ↔ degree φ = 1 := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ h.degree_eq_one φ id rfl, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  have hinj : Injective φ := by
    simpa using (biholomorphOfDegreeEqOne φ h).injective
  exact isSimpleSphere_of_injOn (z := (∞ : OnePoint ℂ)) univ_mem hinj.injOn fun _ hw ↦ hinj hw

/-- For `n ≥ 2` the power map `z ↦ z ^ n` of the Riemann sphere, of degree `n`, is not simple. -/
theorem not_isSimpleSphere_onePointMap_pow {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) :
    ¬IsSimpleSphere (OnePoint.map fun z : ℂ ↦ z ^ n) := by
  have hn0 : n ≠ 0 := by omega
  rw [← FiniteHolomorphicMap.coe_spherePow hn0, isSimpleSphere_iff_degree_eq_one,
    FiniteHolomorphicMap.coe_spherePow, degree_onePointMap_pow]
  omega

/-! ### Rotation invariance and the power maps -/

/-- **Maps invariant under the `n`-th roots of unity factor through `z ↦ z ^ n`.** If `u` is
invariant under the rotations `z ↦ ζ z` by the `n`-th roots of unity, then `u = v ∘ φ` for the
power map `φ (z) = z ^ n` of the sphere and some `v`. -/
theorem exists_eq_comp_onePointMap_pow {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0)
    (h : ∀ ζ : ℂ, ζ ^ n = 1 → ∀ z : ℂ, u ((ζ * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) :
    ∃ v : OnePoint ℂ → X, u = v ∘ OnePoint.map fun z : ℂ ↦ z ^ n := by
  choose r hr using fun y : ℂ ↦ IsAlgClosed.exists_pow_nat_eq y (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hn)
  refine ⟨fun y ↦ y.elim (u (∞ : OnePoint ℂ)) fun y ↦ u (r y), funext fun z ↦ ?_⟩
  induction z using OnePoint.rec with
  | infty => rfl
  | coe z =>
    simp only [comp_apply, OnePoint.map_some, OnePoint.elim_some]
    by_cases hz : z = 0
    · have hr0 : r (z ^ n) = 0 := by
        have := hr (z ^ n)
        rw [hz, zero_pow hn] at this ⊢
        exact pow_eq_zero_iff hn |>.1 this
      rw [hr0, hz]
    · have := h (r (z ^ n) / z) (by rw [div_pow, hr, div_self (pow_ne_zero n hz)]) z
      rwa [div_mul_cancel₀ _ hz, eq_comm] at this

/-- A map invariant under the rotations by the `n`-th roots of unity, for some `n ≥ 2`, is not
simple: it factors through `z ↦ z ^ n`. -/
theorem not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_pow_eq_one {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n)
    (h : ∀ ζ : ℂ, ζ ^ n = 1 → ∀ z : ℂ, u ((ζ * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) :
    ¬IsSimpleSphere u := by
  have hn0 : n ≠ 0 := by omega
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_comp_onePointMap_pow hn0 h
  have hdeg : 1 < degree (FiniteHolomorphicMap.spherePow hn0) := by
    rw [FiniteHolomorphicMap.coe_spherePow, degree_onePointMap_pow]
    omega
  rw [← FiniteHolomorphicMap.coe_spherePow hn0]
  exact not_isSimpleSphere_comp hdeg v

/-! ### Stabilizers of continuous simple spheres -/

/-- If `u` is invariant under `z ↦ a z` with `a ≠ 0`, it is invariant under every integer power. -/
private theorem apply_zpow_mul_eq {a : ℂ} (ha : a ≠ 0)
    (h : ∀ z : ℂ, u ((a * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) (k : ℤ) (z : ℂ) :
    u ((a ^ k * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := by
  have hnat : ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : ℂ), u ((a ^ n * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := by
    intro n
    induction n with
    | zero => simp
    | succ n ih => intro z; rw [pow_succ', mul_assoc, h, ih]
  rcases Int.eq_nat_or_neg k with ⟨n, rfl | rfl⟩
  · simpa using hnat n z
  · rw [zpow_neg, zpow_natCast, ← hnat n, ← mul_assoc, mul_inv_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero n ha),
      one_mul]

section Stabilizer

variable [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X]

/-- A continuous simple sphere is not constant on the affine points `ℂ`, since these are dense. -/
private theorem IsSimpleSphere.not_forall_coe_eq (hu : IsSimpleSphere u) (hc : Continuous u)
    (x : X) : ¬∀ z : ℂ, u z = x := fun h ↦ by
  obtain ⟨w₁, w₂, hne⟩ := hu.nonconstant
  have := denseRange_coe.equalizer hc continuous_const (funext h)
  exact hne (by rw [congrFun this w₁, congrFun this w₂])

/-- If `u` takes the value `x` along a sequence converging to `p`, and `u` is continuous, then
`u p = x`. -/
private theorem eq_apply_of_tendsto (hc : Continuous u) {s : ℕ → OnePoint ℂ} {p : OnePoint ℂ}
    {x : X} (hs : Tendsto s atTop (𝓝 p)) (h : ∀ k, u (s k) = x) : x = u p :=
  tendsto_const_nhds_iff.1 (((hc.tendsto p).comp hs).congr h)

/-- A continuous simple sphere is not invariant under a nonzero translation `z ↦ z + b`: the
translates `z + k b` of each point tend to `∞` as `k → ∞`, so such a map is constant. -/
private theorem not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_add (hc : Continuous u) {b : ℂ} (hb : b ≠ 0)
    (h : ∀ z : ℂ, u ((z + b : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) : ¬IsSimpleSphere u := by
  intro hu
  have hk : ∀ (k : ℕ) (z : ℂ), u ((z + k * b : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := by
    intro k
    induction k with
    | zero => simp
    | succ k ih => intro z; rw [Nat.cast_succ, add_one_mul, ← add_assoc, h, ih]
  have hinf : ∀ z : ℂ, u z = u (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) := fun z ↦ by
    have hnorm : Tendsto (fun k : ℕ ↦ (k : ℝ) * ‖b‖ - ‖z‖) atTop atTop :=
      tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ _
        (tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop.atTop_mul_const (norm_pos_iff.2 hb))
    have ht : Tendsto (fun k : ℕ ↦ z + k * b) atTop (coclosedCompact ℂ) := by
      rw [coclosedCompact_eq_cocompact, ← Metric.cobounded_eq_cocompact,
        ← tendsto_norm_atTop_iff_cobounded]
      refine tendsto_atTop_mono (fun k ↦ ?_) hnorm
      have := norm_sub_norm_le ((k : ℂ) * b) (-z)
      rw [norm_mul, Complex.norm_natCast, norm_neg, sub_neg_eq_add, add_comm] at this
      exact this
    exact eq_apply_of_tendsto hc ((tendsto_coe_infty (X := ℂ)).comp ht) fun k ↦ hk k z
  exact hu.not_forall_coe_eq hc _ hinf

/-- A continuous map invariant under a rotation `z ↦ a z`, `|a| = 1`, `a ≠ 1`, is invariant under
all the `n`-th roots of unity for some `n ≥ 2`: those generated by `a` when `a` has finite order,
and `±1` otherwise, as the powers of `a` are then dense in the circle. -/
private theorem exists_two_le_forall_pow_eq_one (hc : Continuous u) {a : ℂ} (ha1 : a ≠ 1)
    (heq : ‖a‖ = 1) (hk : ∀ (k : ℤ) (z : ℂ), u ((a ^ k * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) :
    ∃ n, 2 ≤ n ∧ ∀ ζ : ℂ, ζ ^ n = 1 → ∀ z : ℂ, u ((ζ * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := by
  by_cases hfin : IsOfFinOrder a
  · -- The powers of `a` are the `n`-th roots of unity, `n = orderOf a ≥ 2`.
    have hn : 2 ≤ orderOf a := by
      have := orderOf_pos_iff.2 hfin
      have : orderOf a ≠ 1 := fun h1 ↦ ha1 (orderOf_eq_one_iff.1 h1)
      omega
    refine ⟨orderOf a, hn, fun ζ hζ z ↦ ?_⟩
    have : NeZero (orderOf a) := ⟨by omega⟩
    obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := (IsPrimitiveRoot.orderOf a).eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one hζ
    simpa using hk i z
  · -- The powers of `a` are dense in the circle, so `u` is invariant under `-1`.
    set c : Circle := ⟨a, mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm.2 heq⟩
    have hcfin : ¬IsOfFinOrder c := fun hc' ↦
      hfin (by simpa [c] using Circle.coeHom.isOfFinOrder hc')
    have hclosed : IsClosed {μ : Circle | ∀ z : ℂ, u ((μ * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z} := by
      rw [Set.ofPred_forall]
      exact isClosed_iInter fun z ↦ isClosed_eq (hc.comp ((continuous_coe (X := ℂ)).comp
        ((continuous_subtypeVal.mul continuous_const)))) continuous_const
    have hrange : range (c ^ · : ℤ → Circle) ⊆
        {μ : Circle | ∀ z : ℂ, u ((μ * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z} := by
      rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩ z
      simp only [Circle.coe_zpow]
      exact hk k z
    have hneg : ∀ z : ℂ, u ((-z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := fun z ↦ by
      have h' := hclosed.closure_subset_iff.2 hrange
        ((Circle.denseRange_zpow_of_not_isOfFinOrder hcfin).closure_range ▸ mem_univ (-1)) z
      rwa [Circle.coe_neg, Circle.coe_one, neg_one_mul] at h'
    refine ⟨2, le_rfl, fun ζ hζ z ↦ ?_⟩
    rcases mul_self_eq_one_iff.1 (by rw [← sq]; exact hζ : ζ * ζ = 1) with rfl | rfl
    · simp
    · simpa using hneg z

/-- **Rotation and dilation invariance.** A continuous simple sphere is not invariant under a map
`z ↦ a z` with `a ≠ 0` and `a ≠ 1`. If `|a| ≠ 1`, the iterates of each point under `a` or `a⁻¹`
converge to `0`, so such a map is constant. If `|a| = 1`, it is invariant under all the `n`-th
roots of unity for some `n ≥ 2`, and so factors through `z ↦ z ^ n`. -/
private theorem not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_mul (hc : Continuous u) {a : ℂ} (ha0 : a ≠ 0)
    (ha1 : a ≠ 1) (h : ∀ z : ℂ, u ((a * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z) : ¬IsSimpleSphere u := by
  intro hu
  have hk := apply_zpow_mul_eq ha0 h
  rcases ne_or_eq ‖a‖ 1 with hne | heq
  · -- Some `c = a ^ (± 1)` has `|c| < 1`, and `u (c ^ k z) = u z` for all `k`.
    obtain ⟨c, hc1, hck⟩ : ∃ c : ℂ, ‖c‖ < 1 ∧ ∀ (k : ℕ) (z : ℂ),
        u ((c ^ k * z : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) = u z := by
      rcases hne.lt_or_gt with hlt | hgt
      · exact ⟨a, hlt, fun k z ↦ by simpa using hk k z⟩
      · refine ⟨a⁻¹, by rwa [norm_inv, inv_lt_one₀ (norm_pos_iff.2 ha0)], fun k z ↦ ?_⟩
        simpa [zpow_neg] using hk (-k) z
    have h0 : ∀ z : ℂ, u z = u ((0 : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) := fun z ↦ by
      have ht : Tendsto (fun k : ℕ ↦ c ^ k * z) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
        simpa using (tendsto_pow_atTop_nhds_zero_of_norm_lt_one hc1).mul_const z
      exact eq_apply_of_tendsto hc (((continuous_coe (X := ℂ)).tendsto 0).comp ht)
        fun k ↦ hck k z
    exact hu.not_forall_coe_eq hc _ h0
  · obtain ⟨n, hn, hζ⟩ := exists_two_le_forall_pow_eq_one hc ha1 heq hk
    exact not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_pow_eq_one hn hζ hu

/-- **Continuous simple spheres have trivial stabilizers.** If `u` is a continuous simple sphere
with values in a Hausdorff space and `u (g • w) = u w` for every `w`, then `g = 1`. -/
theorem IsSimpleSphere.eq_one_of_forall_apply_smul_eq (hu : IsSimpleSphere u) (hc : Continuous u)
    {g : PSL(2, ℂ)} (hg : ∀ w, u (g • w) = u w) : g = 1 := by
  -- Conjugate a fixed point `p` of `g` to `∞`; there `g` becomes the affine map `z ↦ a z + b`.
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := exists_smul_eq_self g
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := MulAction.exists_smul_eq PSL(2, ℂ) (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) p
  have hu' : IsSimpleSphere fun w ↦ u (σ • w) := hu.comp_smul σ
  have hc' : Continuous fun w ↦ u (σ • w) := hc.comp (continuous_const_smul σ)
  have hginf : (σ⁻¹ * g * σ) • (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) = (∞ : OnePoint ℂ) := by
    rw [mul_smul, mul_smul, hσ, hp, ← hσ, inv_smul_smul]
  -- `σ⁻¹ g σ` acts on `ℂ` as the affine map `z ↦ a z + b`, `a ≠ 0`, attached to it.
  obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hab⟩ : ∃ a ≠ (0 : ℂ), ∃ b : ℂ,
      ∀ z : ℂ, (σ⁻¹ * g * σ) • (z : OnePoint ℂ) = ((a * z + b : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ) := by
    classical
    let φ := OnePoint.pglStabilizerInftyEquiv
      ⟨toPGL (σ⁻¹ * g * σ), by rw [MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff, toPGL_smul]; exact hginf⟩
    refine ⟨φ.linear 1, φ.linear.map_ne_zero_iff.2 one_ne_zero, φ 0, fun z ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [← AffineEquiv.apply_eq_linear_one_mul_add, OnePoint.coe_pglStabilizerInftyEquiv_apply,
      toPGL_smul]
  have hcoe : ∀ z : ℂ, u (σ • ((a * z + b : ℂ) : OnePoint ℂ)) = u (σ • (z : OnePoint ℂ)) :=
    fun z ↦ by rw [← hab, mul_smul, mul_smul, smul_inv_smul, hg]
  by_cases ha1 : a = 1
  · subst ha1
    by_cases hb : b = 0
    · -- `σ⁻¹ g σ` acts trivially, so it is the identity.
      have h1 : σ⁻¹ * g * σ = 1 := eq_of_smul_eq_smul fun w ↦ by
        induction w using OnePoint.rec with
        | infty => rw [hginf, one_smul]
        | coe z => rw [hab, hb, one_mul, add_zero, one_smul]
      calc g = σ * (σ⁻¹ * g * σ) * σ⁻¹ := by group
        _ = 1 := by rw [h1]; group
    · exact absurd hu' (not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_add hc' hb fun z ↦ by
        simpa using hcoe z)
  · -- Conjugate the fixed point `c = b / (1 - a)` of `z ↦ a z + b` to `0`.
    set c := b / (1 - a)
    have hfix : a * c + b = c := by
      have h1a : (1 : ℂ) - a ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.2 (Ne.symm ha1)
      simp only [c]
      field_simp
      ring
    refine absurd (hu'.comp_smul (upperRightHom c)) (not_isSimpleSphere_of_forall_mul
      (hc'.comp (continuous_const_smul (upperRightHom c)))
      ha ha1 fun z ↦ ?_)
    simp only [upperRightHom_smul_coe]
    rw [← hcoe (z + c), show a * (z + c) + b = a * z + c by linear_combination hfix]

/-- **The reparametrization action is free on continuous simple spheres.** If `u` is a continuous
simple sphere with values in a Hausdorff space and `u ∘ (g • ·) = u ∘ (h • ·)`, then `g = h`. -/
theorem IsSimpleSphere.eq_of_forall_apply_smul_eq_apply_smul (hu : IsSimpleSphere u)
    (hc : Continuous u) {g h : PSL(2, ℂ)} (hgh : ∀ w, u (g • w) = u (h • w)) : g = h := by
  have := hu.eq_one_of_forall_apply_smul_eq hc (g := g * h⁻¹) fun w ↦ by
    simpa [mul_smul] using hgh (h⁻¹ • w)
  rwa [mul_inv_eq_one] at this

end Stabilizer

end TauCeti
